  "answer": "The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ treated women with immense compassion, mercy, and respect, setting an example for all men. He emphasized the importance of fulfilling women's rights and treating them kindly, considering it an obligation upon men. His concern for women was evident in various situations, such as shortening prayers if he heard a child crying to alleviate the mother's distress, and advising gentleness towards women, likening them to delicate glass vessels. He also dedicated a special day to women to provide them with sermons and advice, and even offered a ride to a woman carrying a heavy load, demonstrating his practical support and care.",
